00073696                            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
00073696                            ; Unused RAM addresses for FM and PSG channel variables used by the Special SFX
00073696                            ; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
00073696                            ; The first block would have been used for overriding the music tracks
00073696                            ; as they have a lower priority, just as they are in Sound_PlaySFX
00073696                            ; The third block would be used to set up the Special SFX
00073696                            ; The second block, however, is for the SFX tracks, which have a higher priority
00073696                            ; and would be checked for if they're currently playing
00073696                            ; If they are, then the third block would be used again, this time to mark
00073696                            ; the new tracks as 'currently playing'
00073696                            
00073696                            ; These were actually used in Moonwalker's driver (and other SMPS 68k Type 1a drivers)
00073696                            
00073696                            ; BGMFM4PSG3RAM:
00073696                            ;SpecSFX_BGMChannelRAM:
00073696 00FF F100                  		dc.l (v_snddriver_ram+v_music_fm4_track)&$FFFFFF
0007369A 00FF F1F0                  		dc.l (v_snddriver_ram+v_music_psg3_track)&$FFFFFF
